msgid "Alcance_del_portafolio"
msgstr "Portfolio Scope"

msgid "portfolio_rios"
msgstr "The system is set to analyze NbS implementation opportunities through the capabilities of the Resource Investment Optimization System (RIOS), which is a model created to provide a standardized approach to watershed management worldwide. It combines biophysical, social and economic data to help users identify the best places to maximize the ecological return on investment, within socially and politically feasible limits."

msgid "portfolio_rios_2"
msgstr "RIOS generates maps, in the form of raster files that show the optimal location for investments in natural infrastructure to maximize the ecological return related to the objectives associated with erosion control, nutrient retention, flood mitigation, biodiversity. Separates transitions and uses information about each in the diagnostic evaluation and portfolio selection process. These transitions include:"

msgid "protection_portfolio"
msgstr "maintain native vegetation (protection)"

msgid "revegetacion_portfolio"
msgstr "Revegetation (without assistance)"

msgid "revegetacion_asistida_portfolio"
msgstr "Revegetation (without assistance)"

msgid "manejo_vegetacion_portfolio"
msgstr "Agricultural vegetation management"

msgid "abertura_portfolio"
msgstr "Ditching"

msgid "manejo_fertilizante_portfolio"
msgstr "Fertilizer management"

msgid "Manejo_pastos_portfolio"
msgstr "Pasture management"

msgid "portfolio_conservation"
msgstr "Forest conservation: Actions aimed at conserving current coverage through the signing of conservation agreements, payment to forest rangers, and fencing of areas. This action does not generate changes in coverage but prevents a decrease in coverage in a no-project scenario."

msgid "portfolio_restauration"
msgstr "Passive restoration: Combination of actions that facilitate the natural regeneration of systems. These actions primarily aim to eliminate the source of degradation of vegetation cover."

msgid "portfolio_Agroforesteria"
msgstr "Agroforestry: Active introduction of productive plants, usually shrubs or trees, often in combination with other species (e.g., shade coffee or cacao with banana)."

msgid "portfolio_active"
msgstr "Active Restoration - Enrichment: Combination of actions aimed at recovering vegetation cover. Strictly speaking, this process seeks to replicate the degraded ecosystem. However, the concept of restoration is often used more flexibly to describe a process of plant enrichment to recover the vegetation cover of a site."

msgid "portfolio_silvopastoriles"
msgstr "Silvopastoral Systems: Active introduction of shrubs and trees to improve soils and provide forage for livestock for greater productivity. This is generally associated with an improvement in previously compacted soils as well as an improvement in pasture quality."

msgid "portfolio_continue"
msgstr "Click the Next button to continue"

msgid "portfolio_alcance_help"
msgstr "Scope of this functionality"

msgid "portfolio_alcance_help_text"
msgstr "In this section, the key actions describe the Nature-based Solutions (NbS) that the RIOS model can analyze and recommend."

msgid "portfolio_alcance_help_text_2"
msgstr "The RIOS model integrates biophysical, social, and economic data to help users identify the best locations for protection and restoration activities. The model maximizes ecological returns on investments, taking into account social and political feasibility."

msgid "portfolio_alcance_help_text_3"
msgstr "RIOS Portfolio Translator uses the results of the Investment Portfolio Advisor to generate scenarios for future conditions. Potential applications of the RIOS model include erosion control of water deposits, nutrient retention, flood mitigation, groundwater recharge, and biodiversity."

msgid "portfolio_analisis_help"
msgstr "This is the final step in configuring your portfolio where the user defines the financial resources available in two ways:"

msgid "portfolio_analisis_text_1"
