msgid "Study case step 4 help 1"
msgstr "This option allows you to include the ocean boundary condition in the flood model if the study area is near the coast."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 2"
msgstr " If you have selected the ocean boundary condition, you must enter the ocean elevation in meters. This value is used to simulate the influence of sea level on flooding in coastal areas."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 3"
msgstr "InVEST calculates the amount of carbon stored in different ecosystem components, which is essential for evaluating the environmental benefits of Nature-based Solutions (NbS)."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 4"
msgstr "Refers to the land use and land cover category for each area. "

msgid "Study case step 4 help 5"
msgstr "Amount of carbon stored in aboveground vegetation biomass, measured in megagrams per hectare (Mg/ha)."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 6"
msgstr "Carbon stored in the roots and belowground biomass."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 7"
msgstr "Amount of carbon stored in the soil."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 8"
msgstr "Refers to carbon stored in dead organic matter, such as fallen leaves or dead wood."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 9"
msgstr "These curves are used to estimate the economic damages caused by flooding in different sectors. Damage factors (fraction of maximum damage cost) are calculated based on water depth and applied to five land use categories: residential, commercial, industrial, transportation infrastructure, and agriculture. "

msgid "Study case step 4 help 10"
msgstr "Represents the maximum economic damage that can occur in the study area as a result of flooding. This value is used in conjunction with the depth-damage curves to estimate expected losses."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 11"
msgstr "Select the currency to be used for calculating costs and damages. "

msgid "Study case step 4 help 12"
msgstr "Show how flood impact varies across different land use types as flood depth increases."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 13"
msgstr "Indicates the depth of flooding in meters, which determines the severity of the flood event. For each depth level, damages will be calculated for the predefined sectors: residential, commercial, industrial, transportation infrastructure, and agriculture."

msgid "Study case step 4 help 14"
msgstr "You will be asked to specify the percentage of non-residential area allocated to commercial and industrial use in the study area. This helps to more accurately determine the economic damages in affected areas."

