# WaterProof Parameter Customization Translations

msgid "parameter_customization_title"
msgstr "Parameter Customization - WaterProof"

msgid "parameter_customization_description"
msgstr "In this section, you can customize the parameters of the models and relationships that WaterProof uses to estimate benefits from flood mitigation and carbon storage."

msgid "ocean_boundary_condition_title"
msgstr "Ocean Boundary Condition"

msgid "ocean_boundary_condition_description"
msgstr "This option is designed for coastal areas where interaction with the sea influences flood levels. If you enable this option, you must enter the ocean elevation (in meters) that you want to consider for the analysis. WaterProof will use this value as a boundary condition to simulate sea level influence."

msgid "exponential_relationship_title"
msgstr "Exponential Relationship Parameters"

msgid "exponential_relationship_description"
msgstr "This option allows WaterProof to understand how the morphological conditions of the river (channel width and depth) change within the analysis basin as the drainage area increases. This uses allometric hydraulic relationships."

msgid "exponential_relationship_enable_description"
msgstr "If you enable this option, you must enter:"

msgid "allometric_hydraulic_parameters"
msgstr "Values for the allometric hydraulic relationship parameters for river width and depth"

msgid "width_mul_parameter"
msgstr "Width mul - Scaling for exponential channel width law"

msgid "width_exp_parameter"
msgstr "Width exp - Exponent for exponential channel width law"

msgid "depth_mul_parameter"
msgstr "Depth mul - Scaling for exponential channel depth law"

msgid "depth_exp_parameter"
msgstr "Depth exp - Exponent for exponential channel depth law"

msgid "min_cross_section_parameter"
msgstr "Min cross section: Minimum cross-section area for channel to be included as channel cell"

msgid "channel_mannings_parameter"
msgstr "Channel Mannings: Default Manning coefficient for rivers"

msgid "carbon_storage_title"
msgstr "Carbon Storage and Sequestration (InVEST)"

msgid "carbon_storage_description"
msgstr "InVEST calculates the amount of carbon stored in different ecosystem components, which is essential for evaluating the environmental benefits of Nature-based Solutions (NbS)."

msgid "required_parameters_title"
msgstr "Required parameters:"

msgid "lulc_code_parameter"
msgstr "LULC Code: Land use and land cover category for each area"

msgid "c_above_parameter"
msgstr "C_above (Mg/ha): Carbon stored in aboveground plant biomass"

msgid "c_below_parameter"
msgstr "C_below (Mg/ha): Carbon stored in roots and belowground biomass"

msgid "c_soil_parameter"
msgstr "C_soil (Mg/ha): Carbon stored in soil"

msgid "c_dead_parameter"
msgstr "C_dead (Mg/ha): Carbon stored in dead organic matter (fallen leaves, dead wood)"

msgid "flood_depth_damage_title"
msgstr "Flood Depth-Damage Functions"

msgid "flood_depth_damage_description"
msgstr "These functions relate flood depth to damage costs to estimate economic losses across different sectors: residential, commercial, industrial, infrastructure, and agriculture."

msgid "maximum_damage_costs_title"
msgstr "Maximum Damage Costs"

msgid "maximum_damage_costs_description"
msgstr "Represents the maximum possible economic damage cost from flooding in the study area. You can select the currency to enter the costs. These values are combined with depth-damage curves to estimate expected losses."

msgid "damage_factor_functions_title"
msgstr "Damage Factor Functions"

msgid "damage_factor_functions_description"
msgstr "Represent how flood damage costs vary between different sectors as depth increases. The curves are constructed by specifying:"

msgid "flood_depth_specification"
msgstr "Flood depth (in meters) to determine event severity"

msgid "calculated_damages_specification"
msgstr "Calculated damages for each sector: residential, commercial, industrial, transportation infrastructure, and agriculture"

msgid "non_residential_percentage_title"
msgstr "Percentage of Non-Residential Area"

msgid "non_residential_percentage_description"
msgstr "Specify what percentage of the total area corresponds to residential and non-residential use. This information improves the accuracy of economic damage calculations in affected areas."

msgid "Fastflood hydrograph description"
msgstr "This hydrograph shows the variation of water discharge in the watershed over time. The three lines represent different scenarios: Current shows the current conditions of the watershed, BAU (Business As Usual) projects the flow without implementing solutions, and NbS (Nature-based Solutions) shows how the implementation of nature-based solutions can reduce and regulate discharge, helping to mitigate floods. You can also select the return period and observe how the peak flow and overall discharge change under different rainfall intensities."

msgid "Fastflood mitigationgeographic description"
msgstr "Visualize and compare flood maps under the Current, BAU (Business As Usual), and NbS (Nature-based Solutions) scenarios. Use the controls to select a variable (maximum water level, peak discharge, or velocity) and the return period (2, 5, 10, 20… up to 1000 years) you want to analyze. Zoom in on areas of interest to explore in detail how nature-based solutions can help reduce flood risks."

msgid "help_description_list_cases_study_fastflood_1"
msgstr "To create your case study, you must complete several steps, starting with the selection of the watershed (area of interest), indicating whether you want the system to perform a carbon market analysis, selecting the Nature-based Solutions (NbS) you wish to implement in those areas, and entering an estimated budget for each proposed solution. This will allow the system to calculate the ROI."

msgid "help_description_list_cases_study_fastflood_2"
msgstr "Remember that ROI (Return on Investment) is an indicator that shows how much money is gained or lost from the investments made. It is a performance measure used to evaluate the efficiency of an investment or to compare the efficiency of multiple different investments."